CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ const array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ T is the unqualified array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ array of arrays of const int: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ non-const array: primary: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.type.qualifier]/3, [temp.deduct.type]/1: an array of const char
is "const T" with T = char[3].  The front end deduced T = const char[3] (the
const was removed from the array node only), so I<const char[3]> derived
from itself and the type checker recursed without bound in primary_base /
vtable_pointer_component (SIGSEGV, bin53).  libstdc++'s
incrementable_traits<const _Tp> : incrementable_traits<_Tp> takes this path
for the type of a string literal (std::format("{}", 42),
cpp11_libstdcxx_header_drops/test_format.desc).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
